[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2710054290","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103896#issuecomment-2710054290","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103896","id":2710054290,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hiCWS","user":{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-10T10:10:15Z","updated_at":"2025-03-10T10:10:15Z","body":"It makes sense to me, but why introduce a new word for it? Why not have a utility function called `thread_await` or `await_thread` instead of either a utility function called `thread_suspend` or a keyword?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2710054290/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2710067343","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103896#issuecomment-2710067343","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103896","id":2710067343,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hiFiP","user":{"login":"reduz","id":6265307,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyNjUzMDc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6265307?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz","html_url":"https://github.com/reduz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-10T10:14:37Z","updated_at":"2025-03-10T10:14:37Z","body":"@aaronfranke to me awaiting on script is saving the call stack and then restoring it. Suspending a thread is stopping executing until something resumes it. Feels like different words for different concepts to me.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2710067343/reactions","total_count":6,"+1":6,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2710083684","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103896#issuecomment-2710083684","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103896","id":2710083684,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hiJhk","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-10T10:20:25Z","updated_at":"2025-03-10T10:20:25Z","body":"Maybe it's better to have this be another static method on `Thread` instead, like `Thread.suspend_until`, to avoid adding more to the global namespace?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2710083684/reactions","total_count":7,"+1":7,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2710589603","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103896#issuecomment-2710589603","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103896","id":2710589603,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hkFCj","user":{"login":"reduz","id":6265307,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyNjUzMDc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6265307?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz","html_url":"https://github.com/reduz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-10T13:24:40Z","updated_at":"2025-03-10T13:24:40Z","body":"@bruvzg makes sense, should probably add an optional argument for connecting on main thread and making it default.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2710589603/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2711387463","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103896#issuecomment-2711387463","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103896","id":2711387463,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hnH1H","user":{"login":"radiantgurl","id":69520693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5NTIwNjkz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69520693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/radiantgurl","html_url":"https://github.com/radiantgurl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radiantgurl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radiantgurl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radiantgurl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radiantgurl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radiantgurl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radiantgurl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radiantgurl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radiantgurl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radiantgurl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-10T17:52:10Z","updated_at":"2025-03-10T17:52:10Z","body":"Maybe we should first make signals multi-threaded first? https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99697","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2711387463/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2711766090","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103896#issuecomment-2711766090","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103896","id":2711766090,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hokRK","user":{"login":"sockeye-d","id":106356149,"node_id":"U_kgDOBlbdtQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106356149?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d","html_url":"https://github.com/sockeye-d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-10T20:36:51Z","updated_at":"2025-03-10T20:36:51Z","body":"Another function of await is being able to assign a variable the result of the signal. Would that be possible to implement with this method?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2711766090/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2714282900","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103896#issuecomment-2714282900","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103896","id":2714282900,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hyKuU","user":{"login":"reduz","id":6265307,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyNjUzMDc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6265307?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz","html_url":"https://github.com/reduz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-11T13:35:10Z","updated_at":"2025-03-11T13:35:10Z","body":"@radiantgurl The problem of making it thread safe is the performance loss of having to lock a mutex every time you emit. \r\nThis happens because inside of Object, signals are not allocated until connected (which saves a ton of memory). If you want to protect this properly, you have to lock both the signal and the signal map and use quite coarse locking, which is very undesirable and also quite prone to deadlocks. \r\n\r\nTo do it properly, you most likely need to use raw pointers and a chunked list, together with fine grained atomics usage, so adding/removing elements is not as costly. Its doable, but its hard.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2714282900/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2714828143","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103896#issuecomment-2714828143","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103896","id":2714828143,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6h0P1v","user":{"login":"reduz","id":6265307,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyNjUzMDc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6265307?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz","html_url":"https://github.com/reduz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-11T15:44:30Z","updated_at":"2025-03-11T15:44:30Z","body":"@sockeye-d Yes, I fixed up the OP, you have to suspend with the completed signal, because when you await the function returns an actual state object. I think this should be better documented in the engine, but I added a note in the doc in the PR.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2714828143/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2715448833","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103896#issuecomment-2715448833","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103896","id":2715448833,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6h2nYB","user":{"login":"dreed-sd","id":105473261,"node_id":"U_kgDOBklk7Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105473261?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dreed-sd","html_url":"https://github.com/dreed-sd","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dreed-sd/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dreed-sd/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dreed-sd/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dreed-sd/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dreed-sd/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dreed-sd/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dreed-sd/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dreed-sd/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dreed-sd/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-11T19:14:31Z","updated_at":"2025-03-11T19:14:31Z","body":"> it is up to the user to protect and make sure nothing is connecting or emitting while the thread suspends.\r\n\r\nIf I have to acquire a lock to prevent other threads from emitting it in order to use `Thread.suspend`, then how would my thread ever resume, as I'd have the lock while suspended?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2715448833/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2715459470","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103896#issuecomment-2715459470","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103896","id":2715459470,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6h2p-O","user":{"login":"MarianoGnu","id":1776044,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NzYwNDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1776044?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu","html_url":"https://github.com/MarianoGnu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-11T19:19:45Z","updated_at":"2025-03-11T19:19:45Z","body":"There's also a chance that the object meant to emit the signal is destroyed, in that case the thread will remain suspended forever until the application ends?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2715459470/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2717757890","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103896#issuecomment-2717757890","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103896","id":2717757890,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6h_bHC","user":{"login":"reduz","id":6265307,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyNjUzMDc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6265307?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz","html_url":"https://github.com/reduz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-12T12:40:35Z","updated_at":"2025-03-12T12:40:35Z","body":"@dreed-sd If you are connecting to the main thread, you don't need to acquire a lock to prevent other threads from emitting. If you are connecting within threads (second argument being true), I can see this being a problem. \r\n\r\nFor this, one possibility could be to pass an optional mutex as third argument to make the operation safe.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2717757890/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2717970973","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103896#issuecomment-2717970973","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103896","id":2717970973,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iAPId","user":{"login":"MarianoGnu","id":1776044,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NzYwNDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1776044?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu","html_url":"https://github.com/MarianoGnu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-12T13:56:33Z","updated_at":"2025-03-12T13:56:33Z","body":"> For this, one possibility could be to pass an optional mutex as third argument to make the operation safe.\r\n\r\nCould each `Signal` instance have it's own mutex to be used only while connecting? or even having a satic/unique mutex\r\n- With a mutex per signal, threads will only pause during conneciton of 2 threads are connecting to the same signal at the same time\r\n- Wig a mutex per object, threads will only pause if during connection 2 threads are connecting to signals of the same owner object\r\n- With a unique mutex, threads will only stop if they are connecting to any signal at the same time (which usually is unlikely because usually signals are only connected on the main thread)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2717970973/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2810213174","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103896#issuecomment-2810213174","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103896","id":2810213174,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ngHM2","user":{"login":"reduz","id":6265307,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyNjUzMDc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6265307?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz","html_url":"https://github.com/reduz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reduz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-16T17:14:36Z","updated_at":"2025-04-16T17:14:36Z","body":"Just for the record, I added thread safety to signals in #105453. I thought this would be very complex, but it turns out @AThousandShips did most of the work for this. Once that one is merged, it should be possible to merge this one too.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2810213174/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"la